{"availability":"available","full":"Xetnus/osm-finder","name":"osm-finder","description":"A \"line-network\" geolocation tool created for Bellingcat's September 2022 Hackathon: https://www.bellingcat.com/resources/2022/10/06/automated-map-searches-scam-busting-tools-and-twitter-search-translations-here-are-the-results-of-bellingcats-second-hackathon/","category":"Developer tools","language":"Vue","stars":122,"forks":7,"created":"2022-09-24T00:38:12Z","updated":"2023-08-22T01:31:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://osm-finder.netlify.app/","topics":["geolocation","openstreetmap"],"demo":"https://osm-finder.netlify.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:33:53.068Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:33:53.068Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:33:53.068Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:08:07.977Z","stars":122,"forks":7},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:33:53.068Z","stars":122,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["One of the most prominent tools that assists in geolocating images using OpenStreetMap data is Overpass Turbo. This requires learning the Overpass Query Language and restricts your geolocation abilities to only what's permitted by the query language.","This tool attempts to make it easier for researchers to find locations with a simple click-and-drag interface. No need to learn a new query language. It also adds capabilities not present in existing tools, like the ability to find locations by leveraging the angles created by line intersections and the ability to search for uniquely shaped features.","This tool is in beta development. If you encounter any issues or have recommendations on how to improve the application, please feel free to open an issue."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Xetnus/osm-finder/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2f395e67957ffe8ac840a24da39ea6eea192243f3c61f50592b0f675ff3e2b2e","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:08.159Z"},"overviewCheckedA